These cutter heads use TDHB07T1202-PCD and TPGH080201-PCD diamond inserts. Each have CW and CCW versions.

The TPGH insert has an 11 degree top rake. The TDHB does not have a top rake.

The TDHB uses an M2.2x0.45 or a #2-56 torx head insert screw. A #2-56 nut is used. When using the M2.2 screw, tapping the nut with an M2.2 tap will ensure the threads won't bind.
 
The TPGH uses M2.5x0.45 torx head insert screw and M2.5 nuts. 

The TopLock is secured with ABS slurry (Acetone and ABS).  It provides more support for the insert.

Print these with ABS. Gcode files are sliced for a Bambu X1C with a 0.4mm nozzle. Layer height is .08mm.

The image shows the TPGH cutter head with supports for printing.
